---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Fixture from "../../components/Fixture.astro";
import "../../styles/theme-builder.css";
---
<Base title="Theme builder: your colours, live" description="Build an iVOLT theme in the browser: change brand colours, surfaces, radius and font, watch real components update live, and copy the result as CSS.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Theme builder</h1>
    <p>Every colour, radius and font in iVOLT is a token, and every token is a custom property you can override. Change the controls below: the preview updates live and the CSS to copy appears underneath. Nothing is stored or sent anywhere; the values only live in this page until you copy them.</p>
    <p><span class="docs-new">New in 1.1</span> The builder writes only seeds. Hover, pressed, tint, focus ring, glows and both gradients are mixed by iVOLT itself from your primary (<a href="/foundations/tokens-and-themes#oc-title">one-colour theming</a>), so the CSS to copy is a few lines instead of thirty. Links made with the 1.0 builder still open here.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>Source:</strong> <code>tokens/tokens.json</code>. <strong>Output:</strong> plain custom properties. <strong>Stored:</strong> nothing.</p>
    <div class="docs-tb" data-theme-builder>
      <form class="docs-tb__form docs-tb__controls iv-stack" data-tb-form>
        <fieldset class="iv-fieldset">
          <legend class="iv-fieldset__legend">Mode you are editing</legend>
          <div class="iv-checks iv-checks--inline">
            <label class="iv-check"><input type="radio" name="theme" value="light"> Light</label>
            <label class="iv-check"><input type="radio" name="theme" value="dark" checked> Dark</label>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset class="iv-fieldset">
          <legend class="iv-fieldset__legend">Colours</legend>
          <div class="docs-tb__grid">
            <label class="docs-tb__color"><input type="color" name="primary"> Primary</label>
            <label class="docs-tb__color"><input type="color" name="on-primary" aria-describedby="tb-ratio"> Text on primary</label>
            <label class="docs-tb__color"><input type="color" name="accent"> Accent</label>
            <label class="docs-tb__color"><input type="color" name="bg"> Background</label>
            <label class="docs-tb__color"><input type="color" name="surface"> Surface</label>
            <label class="docs-tb__color"><input type="color" name="surface-raised"> Raised surface</label>
            <label class="docs-tb__color"><input type="color" name="text"> Text</label>
          </div>
          <p class="docs-tb__ratio" id="tb-ratio" data-tb-ratio role="status" data-label-ok="Text on primary: {ratio}:1" data-label-low="Text on primary: {ratio}:1, under 4.5:1. Pick another ink or a deeper primary."></p>
          <p class="iv-field__help iv-u-m-0">Light and dark are kept apart: set one, switch the mode above, set the other. A new primary brings the ink that reads better on it (white or deep navy) until you pick one yourself.</p>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="iv-field">
          <label class="iv-label" for="tb-radius">Corner radius (medium)</label>
          <input class="iv-range" id="tb-radius" name="radius" type="range" min="0" max="1.5" step="0.125" value="0.5">
          <p class="iv-field__help iv-u-m-0">Small and large radii follow proportionally.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="iv-field">
          <label class="iv-label" for="tb-font">Sans-serif stack</label>
          <select class="iv-select" id="tb-font" name="font" data-iv-native>
            <option value='system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif'>System (default)</option>
            <option value='"Outfit", system-ui, sans-serif'>Outfit, then system</option>
            <option value='Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif'>Georgia (serif)</option>
            <option value='ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace'>Monospace</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="iv-cluster">
          <button class="iv-button iv-button--secondary iv-button--sm" type="button" data-tb-reset>Reset</button>
          <button class="iv-button iv-button--primary iv-button--sm" type="button" data-tb-share data-label-done="Link copied" hidden>Copy share link</button>
          <button class="iv-button iv-button--secondary iv-button--sm" type="button" data-tb-download hidden>Download theme.css</button>
          <a class="iv-button iv-button--ghost iv-button--sm" href="/themes">Start from a preset</a>
        </div>
      </form>
      <div class="docs-tb__preview iv-root" data-iv-theme="dark" data-tb-preview>
        <h2 class="iv-u-sr-only">Live preview</h2>
        <Fixture name="card/basic" title="Preview: card" />
        <Fixture name="form/basic" title="Preview: form" />
        <Fixture name="button/variants" title="Preview: buttons" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <Section title="Your overrides" num={1} lead={`Paste this after ivolt.css, or inside @layer iv.overrides when you use the layered stylesheet. One block per mode you changed, and the dark one again for data-iv-theme="system" when the system is dark, so a light/dark switch keeps working. Nested scopes work too: any element with data-iv-theme takes the block of its mode.`}>
      <div class="docs-code-block" data-code-block>
        <div class="docs-code__panel" data-code-panel="css">
          <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Theme overrides CSS"><code id="tb-output" data-tb-output>/* tokens.overrides.css — change a control to see the overrides here. */</code></pre>
          <button class="iv-button iv-button--secondary iv-button--sm docs-copy docs-code__copy" type="button" data-copy-target="tb-output" aria-describedby="tb-output-status">Copy CSS</button>
          <span class="iv-u-sr-only" id="tb-output-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section title="What this does not do" num={2}>
      <ul>
        <li>It edits a handful of tokens. The full set lives in <code>tokens.json</code> and <code>tokens.css</code>; anything can be overridden the same way.</li>
        <li>It measures one pair for you, the text on the primary button, at rest and on hover. Everything else, test with the accessibility tooling of your choice; the shipped themes are tested with axe.</li>
        <li>It does not rebuild the package. Overrides are enough for most brands; a fork of <code>tokens.json</code> is the path for a full palette.</li>
      </ul>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>
<script>
  import { mountThemeBuilder } from "../../scripts/theme-builder.js";
  let teardown = () => {};
  const mount = () => { teardown(); const root = document.querySelector("[data-theme-builder]"); teardown = root ? mountThemeBuilder(root) : () => {}; };
  // The router's page-load event can fire before this page module runs on a hard load: mount now, and again on every navigation.
  mount();
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", mount);
  document.addEventListener("astro:before-swap", () => teardown());
</script>
